  "description": "Erection of 6 storey building providing ground floor commercial unit (Use class E) and 7 flats on upper floors (Use class C3) consisting of 4 x 1 bed 2 person, 2 x 2 bed 4 person and 1 x 3 bed 4 person units, following the demolition of existing buildings.",
  "subdivision_of_building": null,
  "actual_completion_date": null,
  "lpa_app_no": "2024/1260",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "application_type_full": "Full planning permission",
  "last_updated_by": "Portal",
  "appeal_status": null,
  "id": "Hackney-2024_1260",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;span id=&quot;docs-internal-guid-a3689eb2-7fff-c9ed-91ac-917590045e85&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;&quot;&gt;By reason of the proposed development’s proximity to an established late-night music venue, in the absence of a Noise Impact Assessment capturing a live music event at The MOTH Club, it has failed to be demonstrated that the proposed development would not give rise to undue noise and disturbance to future occupiers. The proposed development would, therefore, conflict with Policy D13 of the London Plan and Policy LP2 of the Hackney Local Plan and the NPPF Policy P4 .&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;",
    "The&amp;nbsp;&lt;span id=&quot;docs-internal-guid-2a2b1a3c-7fff-6f17-1f1f-171e386aed22&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;&quot;&gt;proposed development, by reason of a lack of provision of affordable housing, would fail to adequately contribute towards the provision of mixed and balanced communities and housing needs in the local area. As such, the development would not be consistent with policies H4 and H5 of the London Plan (2021), policies LP12 and LP13 of the Hackney Local Plan 2033 (2020), and the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;&quot;&gt;Hackney S106 Planning Contributions Supplementary Planning Document (2020).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;In&amp;nbsp;the absence of a Unilateral Undertaking or a Section 106 agreement securing appropriate mitigation by restricting future occupiers of the development from obtaining parking permits within the Controlled Parking Zone the proposed development would likely exacerbate existing parking stress and congestion on the surrounding highway network. The application is, therefore, contrary to Policy LP45 of the Hackney Local Plan 2033 (2020) and Policy T6 of the London Plan (2021).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;docs-internal-guid-38b09ce9-7fff-ea98-272a-8b0a152f0b1d&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;&quot;&gt;In the absence of a legal agreement securing the financial contribution towards carbon off-setting having been submitted or completed, the proposal would fail to secure&amp;nbsp; financial contribution towards carbon offsetting; resulting in an unacceptable level of carbon dioxide emissions, contrary to policy LP55 of the Hackney Local Plan 2033 (2020).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
